#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-landingpage.rst:7
#: 252fb278243e4e56b495c83fd939fb7a
msgid "Copter/Plane/Rover support a number of different rangefinders including Lidars (which use lasers or infra-red beams for distance measurements), 360 degree Lidars (which can detect obstacles in multiple directions) and Sonars (which use ultrasonic sound). This category also includes Maxbotix Sonar and Pulsed Light LED range finders. These devices can be used for measuring distance near to  the ground for precision landings and altitude control, water depth, or object distance as proximity sensors for :ref:`Object Avoidance<common-object-avoidance-landing-page>`. Vision systems (see :ref:`common-realsense-depth-camera`) can also be used for Object Avoidance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-landingpage.rst:9
#: 53b110dc988449f7a059a88fca0f6a69
msgid "A forward facing rangefinders can also be used for Obstacle Avoidance. See Rangefinder :ref:`Setup Overview <common-rangefinder-setup>` to know more."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-landingpage.rst:11
#: 61e5815f74b04e6ea7cace6d57280820
msgid "Many rangefinders are not included in the standard builds. If you get a pre-arm message that it is not being detected on power up, check the firmware's included :ref:`features list <common-limited_firmware>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-landingpage.rst:18
#: c95f6d0eeda048f3a1c45a5a3349a06c
msgid "Downward facing rangefinders are automatically used in flight modes which have height control, such as Altitude Hold, Loiter and PosHold Mode.  The data from the sensor will be used until you exceed ``RNGFNDx_MAX``, after that it switches to the barometer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-landingpage.rst:23
#: 7dfeb2b2757948b996b37f848d797831
msgid "Copter includes support for :ref:`Terrain Following <terrain-following>` in Auto mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-landingpage.rst:25
#: 7cad674648df40aa9c7030a6c4996941
msgid "Copter can also use rangefinders for :ref:`Object Avoidance <common-object-avoidance-landing-page>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-landingpage.rst:31
#: a816bc85e3fc4305ab0b0e491479c9e6
msgid "``RNGFNDx_MAX`` must be set to a tested, appropriate value.  If ``RNGFNDx_MAX`` is set to a value greater than the range of the sensor, the autopilot will not respond correctly to the data provided."
msgstr ""

